content:
{
  "email": "mei.chen@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket from mei.chen: Outlook says mailbox almost full and some emails won't send. Checking mailbox percent_used per KB-010."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, your mailbox is at about 99% of its 50 GB limit, which is why Outlook is warning you and some emails are not sending. Please free up space, then check again:\n\n1. Empty your Deleted Items and Junk Email folders.\n2. Sort your Inbox and Sent Items by size, largest first. Delete what you no longer need, or save large attachments to OneDrive.\n3. If you need to keep older mail, ask us to turn on Online Archive, and move mail older than a year into it.\n\nThe mailbox can take up to an hour to update after cleanup. Once that time has passed, check Outlook again. If it is still above 95% after cleanup, reply to this ticket and we will look at whether your role needs a larger quota.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: mailbox 50,890 MB used of 51,200 MB quota (99.4%), account active, not locked, no sign-in issues. Above 100% sending stops, so this matches the reported send failures. Per KB-010, sent the user the cleanup steps (empty Deleted/Junk, sort by size and offload attachments to OneDrive, Online Archive for mail older than a year). Waiting on the user to complete cleanup and report back. Escalation criteria not met yet: escalate for a quota increase (manager approval) only if usage stays above 95% after cleanup. Did not check device status; not needed for a quota issue. Possible follow-up: if the user reports Outlook not syncing after cleanup, apply KB-009.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
